 largely targeted Brattin rather than the incumbent.\n\nBrattin's campaign has been defined by legal turmoil. After Republicans redrew the map to try to make the seat competitive, the Supreme Court rejected the plan three times, and the race proceeds under the previous boundaries. Lawsuits now seek to replace Brattin as the Republican nominee, and he has described his own campaign as paralyzed. Nearly all expert raters call the seat Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Cleaver's chances around 95 percent. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9884, "margin": 16.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9837, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.981, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.985, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 16.0}]}